{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1300319-v20-dark-ages-how-do-1s-work-on-damage-dice","id":1300319,"title":"V20 Dark Ages How do 1s work on damage dice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-27T10:05:53-07:00","id":1300319,"title":"V20 Dark Ages How do 1s work on damage dice?","content":"The rules entry on this is fairly confusing. It says Damage rolls can never botch. Treat botches as a normal failure. Does the term &quot;botches&quot; refer to any 1 roll or the net result of more 1s than successes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1527-chavyvampire","name":"ChavyVampire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T14:02:40-07:00","id":1300375,"title":"","content":"A defined by the book, a botch is when you roll any 1s and no successes, not the individual 1s. So Damage rolls calculate failure as normal, but there's no special consequence for what would be a botch on a normal roll.<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> I have played with the house rule that damage and soak rolls don't subtract 1s.... and it doesn't really change much. You only really feel it when you can't soak the damage since the average damage goes up a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}